course: dictionary
lesson: 6097
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so look at the clues around it. «Under big cities, electric trains run in tunnels called the Underground, the Tube, the metro or the subway.» The words under big cities and tunnels tell you that a metro is an underground railway.
explain: Metro can also mean a whole city area. In the US, Canada and Australia, «the metro area» means the city and the towns around it. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Different places use different names for the same kind of railway. London says the Tube, New York says the subway, and Paris says the Métro. When you see a different name, look for clues like tunnels, stations or maps to know which railway is meant.
fact: A metro is an underground railway system in a city.
fact: Other names for a metro are the subway (US) and the Underground or the Tube (London).
fact: In the US, Canada and Australia, «metro» can mean the whole city area, including its suburbs.
fact: A «metro map» is a diagram that shows the order of stations and changes, not real distances.
fact: «Metro» is also part of the names of some newspapers, buses and shops.
exercise: «Under big cities, electric trains run in tunnels called the Underground, the Tube, the metro or the subway.» What is a metro? | A small boat for the river | A kind of bus that stops at every farm | A shop that sells maps | *An electric railway that runs in tunnels under a city
exercise: «For years people reported street dogs in Moscow riding metro trains between stops.» Which word tells you that metro trains stop at places along the way? | *between | street | reported | riding
exercise: A friend says, «Let's check the metro map before we go.» What does a metro map show? | Real distances in miles between every station | Weather for the week ahead | Which shops are open | *The order of stations and where you can change lines
test: In London, people often call the metro the what? | Harbour | *The Tube | Pavement | Motorway
test: Which phrase means the city and its suburbs in the US? | the metro train | a metro map | the metro station | *the metro area
exam: Mia says, «Let's take the metro to the stadium.» How will Mia travel? | By boat across the sea | On a farm tractor | *By underground train around the city | By plane to another country
